If you're not chaotic, you may want to #name them later if you want as
many artifacts as possible.  First do as much sacraficing as you need to
get the artifacts of your alignment and the unaligned ones until you have
what you've decaded are the good ones, then keep it up until you have as
many as you think you'll get, then #name them to have as many as possible.
Do this well above the castle.

The reason is that a small fraction (1/25th?) of the weapons randomly
generated in the dungeon are artifacts.  You'll want them to be as nice
as possible and #naming removes possibilities from the mix.

So there are several strategies:

Wizard, #name one as soon as possible.
Chaotic, #name both as soon as possible.
Other artifact collector, #name both before the castle to improve random
generation chances.

